      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I know that each section does the exact same thing, so at the beginning (patchset 5) I code in the previous if condition. \n\nI am confused on what you are actually trying to accomplish now.\n\u003d\u003e This could check TypeC spec Figure 4-16 Connection State Diagram: DRP with Accessory and Try.SRC Support and ch4.5.2.2.10.2 Exiting from Try.SRC State： in try.src state detecting both Rd or Ra should still stay in try.src, this is what I want to implement. The previous if conditions detecting both Rd or Ra on the cc pins will go to SRC_DISCONNECTED_DEBOUNCE, but when we are in try.src state this transition happens too and does not meet spec (should stay in SRC_DISCONNECTED).  \n\nThis full logical superset is used for unattached.src state. In unattached.src state (TrySource disable in SRC_DISCONNECT) detect resistance of the previous if conditions, it should transit state to SRC_DISCONNECTED_DEBOUNCE. Also we embed try.src in SRC_DISCONNECT by TrySource flag enabled, but the only one Rd on cc pins can transit state to SRC_DISCONNECTED_DEBOUNCE.",
